(￼-dim) feature space.","targetRectangle":{"y":376.22688437444782,"x":173.49999956130978,"width":1452.0761024299068,"height":92.379920690126539}},{"text":"Importance:\\t","targetRectangle":{"y":469.6232088731681,"x":173.49999956130978,"width":223.50000043869022,"height":71.183596954345603}},{"text":"Hilbertian metrics admit positive definite kernels, i.e., can write them as ￼ for a PSD kernel ￼, eg by taking ￼","targetRectangle":{"y":541.82320963610755,"x":223.50000095367432,"width":1509.3944527766221,"height":98.341683838660742}},{"text":"Many efficient algorithms (kernel methods, random projections, convex opt) rely on this.","targetRectangle":{"y":640.98248991031517,"x":223.50000095367432,"width":1141.8660000000004,"height":48.782403945922852}},{"text":"Examples:\\t","targetRectangle":{"y":690.58249029178489,"x":173.49999956130978,"width":223.50000043869022,"height":71.183596954345717}},{"text":"Hilbertian: MMD (by construction!), Energy, Hellinger, ￼","targetRectangle":{"y":762.78249105472435,"x":223.50000095367432,"width":724.61737956356853,"height":48.673863795014881}},{"text":"Non-Hilbertian: ￼ in ￼, TV, KL, JS (and most other ￼-divergences)","targetRectangle":{"y":812.2739512852861,"x":223.50000095367432,"width":928.4031826887981,"height":62.624392537151607}},{"text":"Takeaway: Hilbertian ￼ kernelizable ￼ statistically efficient; non-Hilbertian ￼ harder to approximate","targetRectangle":{"y":875.71594025798458,"x":173.49999956130978,"width":1590.1035745794393,"height":78.509920327730242}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":323.32632337338453,"x":904.38676966179571,"width":462.01786020470979,"height":51.919445278407011}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":826.87395166675583,"x":965.55437803499581,"width":9.8056056074766502,"height":41.373863604280018}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y":198.2482738494873,"x":1463.8483810424805,"width":16.703999999999951,"height":14.463999999999999}},{"text":"equation.pdf","targetRectangle":{"y